body:
I believe that this was actually already feasible, since we're calling `getFacetValues`, based on this https://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-helper-js/blob/4bc11ed6b6db46b6e0ab3d567aebeed1658d1f83/dist/algoliasearch.helper.js#L8489-L8498

> ``` js
> //get values ordered only by name ascending using the string predicate
> content.getFacetValues('city', {sortBy: ['name:asc']);
> //get values  ordered only by count ascending using a function
> content.getFacetValues('city', {
>   sortBy: function(a, b) {
>     return a.count - b.count;
>   }
> });
> ```
